            "text_bXmypf": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "Heading",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<h3>III. THE MUD</h3>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "h3",
                "font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
                "font_size": "",
                "line_height": "normal",
                "letter_spacing": "normal",
                "case": "none",
                "wrap": "pretty",
                "text_color": "#4d0804",
                "custom_class": "",
                "background": false,
                "background_color": "#00000026",
                "corner_radius": 0,
                "padding-block-start": 0,
                "padding-block-end": 0,
                "padding-inline-start": 0,
                "padding-inline-end": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_tdqgqV": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "Text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Then I became a mother.</p><p>Nothing prepared me for the invisible passage from maiden to mother.</p><p>I prepared for birth with devotion, a midwife, a doula, countless books and practices. Yet no one prepared me for what came after.</p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "custom",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                "font_size": "",
                "line_height": "normal",
                "letter_spacing": "normal",
                "case": "none",
                "wrap": "pretty",
                "text_color": "#220706",
                "custom_class": "",
                "background": false,
                "background_color": "#00000026",
                "corner_radius": 0,
                "padding-block-start": 0,
                "padding-block-end": 0,
                "padding-inline-start": 0,
                "padding-inline-end": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_Wta7VB": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "Text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Those first months were beautiful.<br/>A healthy daughter.<br/>Ocean air.</strong></p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "custom",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                "font_size": "1.25rem",
                "line_height": "normal",
                "letter_spacing": "normal",
                "case": "none",
                "wrap": "pretty",
                "text_color": "#4d0804",
                "custom_class": "",
                "background": false,
                "background_color": "#00000026",
                "corner_radius": 0,
                "padding-block-start": 0,
                "padding-block-end": 0,
                "padding-inline-start": 0,
                "padding-inline-end": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_BPBUeB": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "Text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Palm trees swaying above a hammock where I nursed her beneath the Malibu sky.<br/>From the outside, everything appeared complete.<br/>Yet quietly, something inside me began to disappear.</p><p>Motherhood became both the greatest joy I had ever known and the greatest initiation of my life.<br/>At the height of the pandemic, isolation amplified everything.<br/>I searched for places where mothers belonged, not simply tolerated, but truly welcomed.</p><p>Again and again I encountered the same unspoken message:</p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "custom",
