            "text_KRyafe": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "Text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>That search led me to folk herbalism at the School of the Sacred Wild led by herbalist Marysia Miernowska.</p><p>During the quiet of the pandemic, I found an online community unlike anything I had experienced.<br/>Each month we devoted ourselves to a single plant.</p><p>We drank its tea.<br/>Meditated with it.<br/>Learned its stories. Unlocked old memories with plants my ancestors knew, and something awoke within me. </p><p>The process allowed its medicine to slowly transform me from the inside out.<br/>Most importantly, I never had to choose between my daughter and my own becoming.</p><p>Poppy was always welcome.<br/>She sat beside me.<br/>Played nearby.<br/>Tasted the herbs.<br/>Learned alongside me.</p><p>For the first time, I witnessed a way of living where motherhood wasn't an interruption to spiritual life; it was part of it.</p><p>When it came time to complete my final herbal thesis, I created a rainbow tincture from every color of lotus. A full spectrum of lotus.</p><p>Yet one flower continued calling me back.<br/>The Red Lotus.<br/>Its beauty felt ancient.<br/>Its medicine felt familiar.</p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "custom",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                "font_size": "",
                "line_height": "normal",
                "letter_spacing": "normal",
                "case": "none",
                "wrap": "pretty",
                "text_color": "#220706",
                "custom_class": "",
                "background": false,
                "background_color": "#00000026",
                "corner_radius": 0,
                "padding-block-start": 0,
                "padding-block-end": 0,
                "padding-inline-start": 0,
                "padding-inline-end": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_Ft9YHE": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "Text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<h4><em>Red is the color of roots.<br/>Of blood.<br/>Of birth.<br/>Of the life force carried through generations.</em></h4>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "custom",
                "font": "var(--font-heading--family)",
                "font_size": "1.5rem",
                "line_height": "normal",
                "letter_spacing": "normal",
                "case": "none",
                "wrap": "pretty",
                "text_color": "#4d0804",
                "custom_class": "",
                "background": false,
                "background_color": "#00000026",
                "corner_radius": 0,
                "padding-block-start": 0,
                "padding-block-end": 0,
                "padding-inline-start": 0,
                "padding-inline-end": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_mWtEc9": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "Text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>It reminded me that healing isn't about escaping our lives.<br/>It's about returning more fully to them.</p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "custom",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                "font_size": "",
                "line_height": "normal",
                "letter_spacing": "normal",
                "case": "none",
