            "text_zhyXfP": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "Text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Years later, my daughter and I found ourselves in Egypt.</p><p>A dear friend simply said,<br/>\"Bring Poppy.\"<br/>So I did.</p><p>Together in a large group, we woke before dawn, wrapped ourselves in colored silks, and walked into temples older than memory.</p><p>As the first scarlet light rose across the desert, women gathered in song.</p><p>Poppy danced beside me.<br/>Not as a spectator.<br/>As a participant.</p><p>Watching her there, I realized something profound.<br/>We don't have to pass down only what we inherited.</p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "custom",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                "font_size": "",
                "line_height": "normal",
                "letter_spacing": "normal",
                "case": "none",
                "wrap": "pretty",
                "text_color": "#220706",
                "custom_class": "",
                "background": false,
                "background_color": "#00000026",
                "corner_radius": 0,
                "padding-block-start": 0,
                "padding-block-end": 0,
                "padding-inline-start": 0,
                "padding-inline-end": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_grjarM": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "Text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p><strong>We can pass down what we consciously choose to create.</strong></p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "custom",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                "font_size": "1.25rem",
                "line_height": "normal",
                "letter_spacing": "normal",
                "case": "none",
                "wrap": "pretty",
                "text_color": "#4d0804",
                "custom_class": "",
                "background": false,
                "background_color": "#00000026",
                "corner_radius": 0,
                "padding-block-start": 0,
                "padding-block-end": 0,
                "padding-inline-start": 0,
                "padding-inline-end": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_HFGezy": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "Text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Inside the Temple of Hathor, the goddess of music, beauty, motherhood, joy, and sacred celebration, I felt something ancient awaken.</p><p>Not a memory of the past.<br/>A remembrance of the future.<br/>A vision of women gathering across every generation.<br/>Infants.<br/>Mothers.<br/>Grandmothers.<br/>Elders.<br/>No one excluded.<br/>No stage of womanhood left outside the circle.</p><p>That is the world I want my daughter to inherit.<br/>And that is why Monrosia exists.<br/>Monrosia is more than tea.<br/>More than adornment.<br/>More than ritual.</p><p>It is an invitation to remember that women were never meant to walk these thresholds alone.<br/>To create spaces where beauty becomes belonging.</p><p>Where ritual becomes <em><strong>remembrance.</strong></em><br/>Where motherhood is <em><strong>honored.</strong></em>&nbsp;<br/>Where healing happens in <em><strong>community.</strong></em>&nbsp;<br/>Where every woman is welcomed <em><strong>exactly as she is.</strong></em></p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "custom",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                "font_size": "",
                "line_height": "normal",
                "letter_spacing": "normal",
                "case": "none",
                "wrap": "pretty",
                "text_color": "#220706",
                "custom_class": "",
                "background": false,
                "background_color": "#00000026",
                "corner_radius": 0,
                "padding-block-start": 0,
                "padding-block-end": 0,
                "padding-inline-start": 0,
                "padding-inline-end": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_zFRjmD": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "Text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>The lotus teaches us that beauty is not found despite the mud.<br/><strong>It </strong><em><strong>blooms because of it.</strong></em></p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "custom",
                "font": "var(--font-subheading--family)",
                "font_size": "1.25rem",
                "line_height": "normal",
                "letter_spacing": "normal",
                "case": "none",
                "wrap": "pretty",
                "text_color": "#4d0804",
                "custom_class": "",
                "background": false,
                "background_color": "#00000026",
                "corner_radius": 0,
                "padding-block-start": 0,
                "padding-block-end": 0,
                "padding-inline-start": 0,
                "padding-inline-end": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_Rc94bR": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "Text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p>Our lives are no different.<br/>Every challenge can become fertile ground for wisdom.<br/>Every season can become part of our unfolding.</p>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
                "type_preset": "custom",
                "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                "font_size": "",
                "line_height": "normal",
                "letter_spacing": "normal",
                "case": "none",
                "wrap": "pretty",
                "text_color": "#220706",
                "custom_class": "",
                "background": false,
                "background_color": "#00000026",
                "corner_radius": 0,
                "padding-block-start": 0,
                "padding-block-end": 0,
                "padding-inline-start": 0,
                "padding-inline-end": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_x7wiTN": {
              "type": "text",
              "name": "Text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<h4>This is my offering.<br/>A place to gather.<br/>To heal.<br/>To celebrate.<br/>To remember.<br/>To become.</h4>",
                "width": "100%",
                "max_width": "none",
                "alignment": "left",
